WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:06.150
chuckle I lost my little brother who
died in a random medical accident he was

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:11.639
someone that I always looked after how
do you deal with grief and loss of men

00:00:11.639 --> 00:00:21.720
in your command someone asked me a
similar question that the other day

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.430
someone along the lines of how gonna be
good

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:34.770
when you lose a loved one and that's
definitely a tough question and I almost

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:51.449
replied no it isn't good there's nothing
good in death and and then I started to

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:59.609
remember the people I've lost throughout
my life the memories of them the

00:00:59.609 --> 00:01:09.360
experiences the fun their unique
personalities and everything they've

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:23.549
given me not only in their life but in
their death what their life taught me

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:29.810
and what their death taught me the mark

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:45.220
the mark they had left on me and I
realized I realized that even in death

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:59.660
even in death there is good first of all
I was lucky to have that person in my

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:04.100
life even if it was only for a short
time too short of a time but at least I

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:14.000
got that those unforgettable moments
those precious moments at least I got

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:22.190
those and I got to experience those
times to know of the beauty of their

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:27.910
personality their attitude their outlook
on the world

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:37.880
they were all unique and I'm thankful
for the opportunity that I had to

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:49.360
interact with them even if it was just
for a short amount of time and now comes

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:59.330
death death is horrible and death is
wretched and death is cruel and death

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:14.320
isn't fair and I don't know why the best
people seem to get taken from us first

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:23.200
but the fact is death is inescapable

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:36.000
there is no way out in
death in that death is part of life in

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.980
like the contrast between the darkness
and the light without death then there

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:49.580
is no life and the people that I've lost

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:54.020
they taught me that

00:03:55.370 --> 00:04:05.220
they taught me how precious life is how
blessed we are to have every day to

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:20.360
learn and to grow and to laugh and to
live to live to live every day with

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:29.700
purpose and with passion to wake up in
the morning and be thankful thankful for

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:36.260
that morning and thankful for the
opportunity to go out into the world and

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:46.050
live to live for them for those that
don't have the opportunity for those

00:04:46.050 --> 00:05:09.720
that were stolen away by deaths cruel
hand for them I will live I will cherish

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:25.380
their memory and I will live so let's
cry no more let's mourn no more let's

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:34.370
remember but let's not dwell instead

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:40.680
let's laugh and let's love and let's
embrace and cherish everything that life

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:45.740
is and every opportunity it gives us

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:51.380
live

